// ch11 (round 1 D8, round 2 R2-2 / #2227): a `require ... = #pkg:sha1:`
// pin at the top of an entry .vibe. The lanes disagree about this file:
//   - the FS build lane (what run_probes.sh uses) accepts it -- the
//     probe compiles and prints below (the pin is extracted and, being
//     unused, verifies nothing);
//   - `vibe check <this file>` (the directive below) answers
//     `unexpected token: =` at the pin line, exit 1 -- a parse error
//     for a program the build accepts;
//   - as a .vibex, the run lane says `unknown # directive: pkg`.
// When #2227 lands, all lanes should agree with the build lane.
//! cli: check
require @vibe/core 0.2.0 = #pkg:sha1:0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

fn main with Console {
  println("pin head parsed")
}
